><DIV
CLASS="SECTION"
><H1
CLASS="SECTION"
><A
NAME="TEXTMODE-PROBLEMS"
>6.3. Text-mode is broken in some ancient DOS program</A
></H1
><P
>      If you are using a program written for DOS which seems to use the text-mode but
      doesn't display the text properly, you can try the other VGA BIOS, either
      <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>VGABIOS-lgpl-latest</TT
> or <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>VGABIOS-elpin-2.40</TT
>,
      see the <A
HREF="bochsrc.html#BOCHSOPT-VGAROMIMAGE"
>vgaromimage option</A
>.
    </P
><P
>      <IMG
SRC="../images/undercon.png"> Maybe it is a bug in the LGPL VGA BIOS, but for now, it seems to work.
    </P
></DIV
