><DIV
CLASS="SECTION"
><H1
CLASS="SECTION"
><A
NAME="WINIMAGE"
>8.5. Win32 only: Tools to manipulate disk images</A
></H1
><DIV
CLASS="SECTION"
><H2
CLASS="SECTION"
><A
NAME="AEN3834"
>8.5.1. Winimage</A
></H2
><P
>Someone on the <A
HREF="mailinglist.html#BOCHS-DEVELOPERS"
>bochs-developers mailing list</A
> mentioned that they use a program
called WinImage, from <A
HREF="http://www.winimage.com"
TARGET="_top"
>www.winimage.com</A
>
to read and write disk images (floppy and hard disk).  Winimage is a
commercial product with a 30-day trial.</P
><P
>If anyone wants to write a tutorial, send mail to <A
HREF="mailinglist.html#BOCHS-DEVELOPERS"
>bochs-developers mailing list</A
> and volunteer.</P
></DIV
><DIV
CLASS="SECTION"
><H2
CLASS="SECTION"
><A
NAME="AEN3841"
>8.5.2. DiskExplorer</A
></H2
><P
>This section was contributed by Luca Cassioli and Stanislav Shwartsman</P
><P
>I eventually found what all of you were looking for for a long time: a
freeware, graphical, win32 compatible HardDisk image editor! It can
handle a large variety of formats, but the one you need is VMWARE
2.0 PLAIN DISK: you can import/export to/from Bochs images COMPLETE
DIRECTORIES!</P
><P
>You can find it at
<A
HREF="http://hp.vector.co.jp/authors/VA013937/editdisk/index_e.html"
TARGET="_top"
>http://hp.vector.co.jp/authors/VA013937/editdisk/index_e.html</A
></P
></DIV
><DIV
CLASS="SECTION"
><H2
CLASS="SECTION"
><A
NAME="AEN3847"
>8.5.3. Ben Lunt's MTOOLs for Bochs and Win32 and/or DOS</A
></H2
><P
>Ben Lunt wrote a set of utilities for Dos/Win32 to manipulate flat disk images.</P
><P
>You can find it at
<A
HREF="http://www.fysnet.net/mtools.htm"
TARGET="_top"
>http://www.fysnet.net/mtools.htm</A
></P
><P
>These utilities includes :
<P
></P
><UL
><LI
><P
>        BOCHSRC.EXE "Bochs Resource"
        A utility to create/modify a Bochs resource file.</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MKDOSFS.EXE  "Make DOS FS"
        A utility to create a FAT disk image of specified size.</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MCOPYF.EXE  "Copy From"
        A utility to copy an existing file from a FAT disk image to the current
        directory.</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MDEL.EXE  "Delete file"
        A utility to delete an existing file from a FAT disk image.</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MDIREX.EXE  "Directory Extended"
        A utility to view a FAT disk images directory and FAT contents.</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MGETIMG.EXE  "Get Disk Image"
        A utility to create a disk image from a floppy (multiple formats).</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MBOOTCD.EXE  "Create a CDROM Image with boot options"
        Create a CDROM image capable of booting with only a ROOT and a single file.</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MGETCD.EXE  "Get Disk Image of Physical CD"
        A utility to create a disk image from a CD.</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>        MCDINFO.EXE  "Get CD Info"
        A utility to the info from a CD.  Not much yet, but a little.</P
></LI
></UL
>&#13;</P
></DIV
></DIV
